/** @mainpage Antimony: A modular human-readable, human-writeable model definition language

Antimony is a text-based model definition language originally based on <A class="el" target="_top" HREF="https://jdesigner.sourceforge.net/Site/Jarnac.html">Jarnac</a>, and extended to be fully modular.  Antimony models can be converted to and from SBML, flattening the modularity in the process.  See also: @subpage antimony-why

<h2>References</h2>
- <A class="el" target="_top" HREF="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC13082115/">An article on Antimony version 3</a>.
- <A class="el" target="_top" HREF="https://academic.oup.com/bioinformatics/article/30/7/903/232510">The article on translation efforts</a> using both Antimony and <A class="el" target="_top" HREF="https://www.imagwiki.nibib.nih.gov/physiome/jsim">JSim</a>.
- <A class="el" target="_top" HREF="https://academic.oup.com/bioinformatics/article/25/18/2452/196238">The article on Antimony</a> that introduced the language.

<h2>Downloads</h2>
Current version: @LIBANTIMONY_VERSION_STRING@

<em>All users:</em>
- <A class="el" target="_top" HREF="https://github.com/sys-bio/antimony/releases">Binaries and installers</a>, including QTAntimony (the GUI editor and translator) and the command-line translators.
- <code>pip install antimony</code> installs the Python bindings.

<em>Developers:</em>
- <A class="el" target="_top" HREF="https://github.com/sys-bio/antimony">Source code</a> - a full package including the source code for libAntimony and QTAntimony as well as all documentation.  (You will also need <A target="_top" HREF="http://sbml.org/Software/libSBML">libSBML</a> v5.0.0 or higher to be able to translate to SBML.)
<!-- CellML translation is not currently supported; mention disabled, not deleted.
  You will also need the <A target="_top" HREF="http://www.cellml.org/tools/downloads/cellml_api/releases/1.10">CellML SDK</a> to be able to translate to CellML.
-->

<h2>Information</h2>
<em>All users:</em>
- The <A class="el" target="_top" HREF="https://tellurium.readthedocs.io/en/latest/antimony.html">Antimony Tutorial and Documentation</a> on the Tellurium site.
- The @subpage antimony-tutorial will walk you through creating Antimony files from scratch.
- @subpage antimony-qt (compiled for Windows, MacOS, and Linux)
- @subpage antimony-examples are provided to show some of Antimony's features, including its modularity.
- 1063 @subpage antimony-biomodels (from the originals at <A target="_top" HREF="http://biomodels.net/">BioModels.net</a>).
<!-- CellML translation is not currently supported; page disabled, not deleted.
- 167 sets of @subpage antimony-cellml from the originals at <A target="_top" HREF="http://models.cellml.org/exposure/listing/full-list">CellML.org</a>.
-->
- @subpage antimony-translations gives an overview of Antimony and JSim translation results.

<em>Developers:</em>
- @subpage antimony-installation for installation and compilation instructions.
- The <A class="el" HREF="antimony__api_8h.html">API documentation</a> for incorporating libAntimony into your own projects.
- The @subpage antimony-technical-spec is a reference manual, explicitly describing how to parse Antimony models.


<h2>Contact</h2>
- <A target="_top" HREF="https://github.com/sys-bio/antimony/issues">Report a bug</a> (or request a feature) if you have any issues with Antimony or QTAntimony, whether behaviors or inadequacies of the documentation.</P>
- <A target="_top" HREF="https://github.com/sys-bio/tellurium/discussions/605">Antimony discussions</a> is the place to go for questions or other interactions with the Antimony developers and community.</p>


<p>libAntimony is distributed under the @subpage antimony-license.  The Windows binary includes a <A target="_top" HREF="http://sbml.org/Software/libSBML">libSBML</a> dll, which is released under the <A target="_top" HREF="http://sbml.org/Software/libSBML/docs/cpp-api/">LGPL</a>.  libSBML, in turn, relies on <A target="_top" HREF="http://expat.sourceforge.net/">expat</a>, released under the <A target="_top" HREF="http://www.opensource.org/licenses/mit-license.php">MIT license</a>, the <A target="_top" HREF="http://www.gzip.org/">gzip</a> dll, released under the <A target="_top" HREF="http://www.math.utah.edu/docs/info/gzip_1.html#SEC1">GPL</a>, and a <A target="_top" HREF="http://www.bzip.org/">bzip</a> dll, released under the <A target="_top" HREF="http://www.bzip.org/1.0.5/bzip2-manual-1.0.5.html">BSD</a> license.
<!-- CellML translation is not currently supported; mention disabled, not deleted.
DLLs from the <A target="_top" HREF="http://www.cellml.org/tools/downloads/cellml_api/releases/1.10">CellML API</a> are also included, released under a triple <A target="_top" HREF="https://svn.physiomeproject.org/svn/physiome/pce/trunk/COPYING">GPL, LGPL, and MPL</a> license.
-->
In addition, QTAntimony comes with QT dll's, which are released under the <A target="_top" HREF="http://qt.nokia.com/products/licensing/licensing#qt-gnu-lgpl-v">LGPL</a></P>

